speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, I have a question which should be directed to the Minister of Energy, Mines and Resources. In view of the fact that he is out of the country I will direct it to the Prime Minister. What action does the government intend to take to either eliminate or curtail a fire raging in a mine dump in the town of Springfield which now covers over 50 acres and is estimated to be 40 feet in depth? This is polluting the whole town and is a very serious matter for the 8,000 people who live there.
29180-154}
Inquiries of the Ministry
